drivers: unrest+.5 trouble+.2 era+.1
times: Being in a crowd at a protest or a public gathering that turns tense, and choosing what to do in that minute, comes to about 1 in 6 lives (estimate; far more in years of unrest), set at 6 in 1000 a year from 18 to 29, less after
likelier: a young adult in a town or city, a year of closures, cuts or anger at the council, friends who march
rarer: a remote village, a quiet decade, a person who never goes to a protest
gap: 5-30
tone: mixed
life: public life, community, friends
horizon: moment
roles: friend, neighbour
who: friend
earth: the crowd in the square has waited all afternoon for the council's answer, and at dusk a bottle flies from near the front
scene: All afternoon the crowd has filled the square in front of the town hall, waiting for the council's answer on the closures. At dusk the doors stay shut, a bottle flies from somewhere near the front, and the police line takes a step forward. {friend} grabs {Ns} arm.
scene W: {N} came to be counted, peacefully, not for this. Someone has to keep this a hearing and not a riot.
scene U: {N} looks for the way out of the square, and for who threw that bottle. It did not come from anyone {N} knows.
scene B: The crowd is waiting for someone to tell it what to do next. Whoever does will be remembered.
scene R: The anger in the square is {Ns} anger too, and it is rising fast.
scene G: These are {Ns} neighbours, the families from the street that is closing. {N} will not leave them standing here alone.
- W | link arms with the stewards, and hold the front still and quiet | v: security, conformity | lever: loyalty | sphere: rule.W | chance: 60
- U | lead your friend down the side street before the square closes | act: lead their friend down the side street before the square closes | v: security, self-direction | lever: exit | sphere: rule.U | chance: 60
- B | climb onto the fountain, and tell the crowd where to go next | v: power, stimulation | lever: lead | sphere: rule.B | chance: 60
- R | stay at the front, and chant until the doors open | v: stimulation, self-direction | lever: voice | pushes: institution council | sphere: rule.R | chance: 60
- G | gather the families from your street, and see every one of them home | act: gather the families from their street, and see every one of them home | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: rule.G | chance: 60
- BG | find the councillor you know, and get the street's elders in by the side door | act: find the councillor they know, and get the street's elders in by the side door | v: tradition, power | sphere: rule.BG | chance: 50
- RG | start the town's old song, loud, until the whole square is singing instead | v: tradition, stimulation | sphere: rule.RG | chance: 50
- UR | film the police line and the front calmly, so the truth of the night is kept | v: universalism, self-direction | tech: phone | sphere: rule.UR | chance: 50
- WB | offer the officer in charge three speakers to go in and see the council tonight | v: security, power | lever: voice | pushes: institution council | sphere: rule.WB | chance: 50
- WU | tell the stewards who threw the bottle, and which way they went | v: security, conformity | sphere: rule.WU | chance: 50
works: The square calms, the doors open, and three of the crowd go in to speak; the closures are put off for a month.
works: {N} gets home with everyone {N} came with, and the night is remembered for the singing, not the bottle.
fails: The police clear the square, and {N} spends half the night at the station giving a statement.
fails: The night is on every screen as a riot, and the closures go ahead with the town split over it.
